      "id": "C",
      "text": "(A), (C) and (D) only"
     },
     {
      "id": "D",
      "text": "(B), (C) and (D) only B.2 C.3 D.4 Solution: The correct answer is 2.(B) and (D) only. (A) False: X-rays are electromagnetic waves. (B) True: Electromagnetic waves are transverse, meaning electric and magnetic fields vibrate perpendicular to the direction of propagation. (C) False: They can be polarised, since they are transverse. (D) True: In vacuum, all electromagnetic waves travel with the speed of light $ c = 3 \\times 10^{8} $ m/s."
